=== results/onset/RESULT.md l.1-24 ===
1	# Exact onset for D = 6, ℓ = 2: VERIFIED (BHM-017)
2	
3	*2026-10-22, the bh-modes lead. Registration: `results/onset/PREREG.md` (BHM-016, commit
4	`180824b`, sealed before the run). Run at `180824b`. Every check is exact arithmetic (sympy
5	1.14.0; python-flint 0.9.0 `fmpq`, `fmpz_poly`).*
6	
7	## Exact quantities
8	
9	Parametrisation (PREREG §1, ℓ = 2): w = √(1 − q²) = 7μ/(6 + μ²), s = 7(6 − μ²)/(5(6 + μ²)),
10	μ ∈ [0, 1]; U₋(t·x_H) = F(t, μ)/Den(μ), with F of degree (4, 104) and integer coefficients,
11	and Den > 0 on [0, 1].
12	
13	| Claim | Certified statement |
14	|---|---|
15	| **O1** | g(μ) = F(1, μ) has exactly one root in [0, 1], and it is simple. It is the root of the irreducible factor **10μ³ − 11μ² + 228μ − 45** in an isolating interval of width 5.9·10⁻⁴⁶. Hence **q_*² is a root of 3025Y³ − 31521Y² + 99792Y − 68796**, and **q_* = 0.973056436723622598181546252320768965119704171…** (45 digits; both ends of the isolating interval agree to all printed digits). Inside the registered prediction [0.9730564367, 0.9730564368]. Arb root isolation agrees |
16	| **O2** | U₋(x; q) ≥ 0 for all q ∈ [0, q_*] and x ∈ [0, x_H(q)], with equality only at (q_*, x_H(q_*)). Proof: F > 0 on [0, 7/8] × [μ_lo, 1] and on [7/8, 1] × [μ_c, 1], and ∂F/∂t < 0 on [7/8, 1] × [μ_lo, μ_c], with μ_c = μ_hi + 1/64. Each region needed one Bernstein box |
17	| **O3** | U₋(x_H(q); q) < 0 for all q ∈ (q_*, 1]. So the onset mechanism is the horizon |
18	| **O4** | S5's (6.24) bracket at the horizon is > 0 for q < 3/5, = 0 at q = 3/5, < 0 for q > 3/5 |
19	| **O5** | E0 (S5 (5.63b) at n = 4 equals `TARGET.md`'s U₋), s² = 1 + 4mq²/25, w increasing, Den > 0 |
20	
21	**Supplementary exact check** (sympy `real_roots` on host-2, after the run; not part of the registered
22	run): both cubics are irreducible over ℚ, and each has exactly one real root:
23	- μ_* = 0.19893240974605249258…;
24	- q_*² = 0.94683882904927334931….
